+# TiKV-surfaced DST seed registry (the compounding loop)
+
+**M4.6, #257** — proposal 0015 §"DST and tests" → "Fidelity to ADR-0009 — the
+compounding loop"; architecture §13.1; ADR-0009. This file is a **committed seed
+registry**, authored here and **consumed by the slice-7 / #258 two-implementation
+contract harness** (this slice authors the seed; #258 authors the harness that replays
+it against the pinned second implementation). It is data, not a test — `cargo` ignores
+non-`.rs` files under `tests/`.
+
+## Why this is a registry, not a `#[madsim]` regression test in this slice
+
+The compounding loop promotes *real-cluster surprises* back into the deterministic spine
+"**wherever they manifest through the trait contract**." Two constraints make an
+in-this-slice red→green DST regression impossible without violating an invariant:
+
+1. **DST keeps correctness authority; M4 must NOT re-prove atomicity** (brief invariant;
+   ADR-0009 "a real environment is never used to test correctness the simulation already
+   covers"). A DST test that re-derives exactly-one-winner over an in-memory/redb store
+   re-proves Tier-0's own atomicity — which the iteration-1 attempt did, and which was
+   correctly rejected as decorative (the inner redb `commit` has no `.await`, so under
+   madsim's single-threaded executor no racer interleaves mid-commit).
+
+2. **The fix that would flip a genuine regression lives in forbidden code.** The behavior
+   below is only *observable* through the commit protocol / conflict detection in the
+   metadata backend — code this slice must **not** touch (brief: "does not touch `traits`,
+   `core`, `custodian`, or the metadata backend logic"). A red→green whose green requires
+   editing the backend belongs to the backend's own slice, not here.
+
+So the honest artifact is a **committed, documented known-gap seed** the human adjudicates
+at sign-off (brief Known NEEDS-HUMAN: "Human judges whether a documented known-gap seed
+satisfies the bullet, or whether it is genuinely met by a real discovery"). The live
+Tier-1 cluster run is off-Check/privileged; on the first Check there is no real cluster to
+surface a *live* discovery, so this promotes the **hypothesis** proposal 0015 names
+explicitly, ready for #258 to replay once the privileged Tier job produces a real one.
+
+## SEED-0001 — await-inside-commit interleaving
+
+- **seed:** `17`
+- **status:** `known-gap` (documented hypothesis; NOT yet confirmed by a live Tier-1 run)
+- **trait surface:** `MetadataStore::commit` (`crates/traits/src/lib.rs`)
+- **the redb model's assumption that TiKV breaks:** the M4.1–M4.3 `concurrency.rs`
+  determinism rationale argues each `commit()` is *internally synchronous* — one redb
+  write transaction, **no `.await` inside** — so the scheduler only decides *which* writer
+  commits first. Proposal 0015 §"Pinning the trait" flags this as **not true of a TiKV
+  commit**, which `.await`s network I/O at `get_for_update` / prewrite / commit, yielding
+  the scheduler *mid-commit* and admitting interleavings the redb model never exercised.
+- **what #258 must replay:** drive N concurrent CAS commits through the `MetadataStore`
+  trait against the **pinned second implementation** under a model that yields inside
+  `commit`, and assert the two load-bearing clauses still hold under every interleaving the
+  seed sweep explores — **exactly-one-winner** (proposal 0015 §Q5) and **commit-point
+  linearizability** (ADR-0015 clause 2).
+- **provenance:** promoted from proposal 0015 §"Pinning the trait" (the documented gap),
+  pending a live-cluster confirmation from the privileged Tier-1 Jepsen job.
diff --git a/crates/metadata-tikv/tests/tier1_jepsen_metadata.rs b/crates/metadata-tikv/tests/tier1_jepsen_metadata.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..363181d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/metadata-tikv/tests/tier1_jepsen_metadata.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@
+//! **Tier-1 Jepsen consistency over the metadata swap** (M4.6, #257; proposal 0015
+//! §"DST and tests" → "Jepsen consistency", §"Suggested PR sequence" item 6) — the
+//! realism-ladder Jepsen leg extended across the redb→TiKV **metadata** backend swap.
+//!
+//! The Jepsen line began at M2 over the networked chunkstore path
+//! (`crates/chunkstore-grpc/tests/tier1_jepsen_consistency.rs`) and is extended here
+//! across the backend swap: a nemesis injecting a **real** partition (the runner
+//! `docker compose pause`s a quorum-safe minority of PD nodes, concurrent with this load)
+//! validates the **single-zone** consistency clauses (proposal 0015; ADR-0015):
+//! - **clause 2 — linearizability of the commit point:** a value committed for a key is
+//!   the value every subsequent reader observes (read-after-commit), across the
+//!   partition-and-heal.
+//! - **exactly-one-winner under genuine concurrency:** N racers CAS one key; exactly one
+//!   `Committed`, the rest `Ok(Conflict)`, **zero `Err`** — the losing writer is a
+//!   distinguishable conflict, never a fault (`crates/traits/src/lib.rs` `CommitOutcome`).
+//!
+//! Single-zone only (clause 1 collapses into zonal linearizability; Tier-3/multi-region
+//! does not begin until M9, §13.4).
+//!
+//! **The nemesis is injected by the runner, not simulated here.** `cargo xtask meta-jepsen`
+//! draws a reproducible, quorum-safe partition plan through the `wyrd-testkit`
+//! `SeededMetaFaults` seam, exports the faulted PD node indices in
+//! `WYRD_TIER1_NEMESIS_NODES`, and **actually pauses those PD services** for a fault window
+//! while this test drives its CAS/read load. This body therefore **refuses to run without a
+//! nemesis plan present** — a Jepsen leg that applied no fault would prove nothing (that was
+//! the iteration-1 defect this fixes).
+//!
+//! **Gated** like every tier test: `#[ignore]` + a clean skip when `WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS`
+//! is unset, so `cargo xtask ci` compiles the body but never runs it.
+
+/// The PD endpoints, or `None` when TiKV is not configured — the family-wide skip gate.
+fn pd_endpoints() -> Option<Vec<String>> {
+    match std::env::var("WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS") {
+        Ok(raw) if !raw.trim().is_empty() => Some(
+            raw.split(',')
+                .map(|e| e.trim().to_string())
+                .filter(|e| !e.is_empty())
+                .collect(),
+        ),
+        _ => None,
+    }
+}
+
+/// The faulted PD node indices the runner's nemesis is partitioning (non-empty), or `None`
+/// if no nemesis plan was wired in. A Jepsen run MUST have one.
+fn nemesis_nodes() -> Option<Vec<usize>> {
+    let raw = std::env::var("WYRD_TIER1_NEMESIS_NODES").ok()?;
+    let nodes: Vec<usize> = raw
+        .split(',')
+        .filter_map(|s| s.trim().parse::<usize>().ok())
+        .collect();
+    (!nodes.is_empty()).then_some(nodes)
+}
+
+#[test]
+#[ignore = "Tier-1: needs a real containerized TiKV + fault injection — run via `cargo xtask meta-jepsen`"]
+fn commit_point_linearizable_and_exactly_one_winner_under_partition() {
+    let Some(endpoints) = pd_endpoints() else {
+        eprintln!(
+            "tier1_jepsen_metadata: WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS unset — skipping (clean skip; the \
+             gate stays green without a TiKV). Run `cargo xtask meta-jepsen`."
+        );
+        return;
+    };
+    // A Jepsen run with no injected nemesis proves nothing — refuse it. `cargo xtask
+    // meta-jepsen` always wires the plan; running this target by hand without it is the
+    // configuration error we surface loudly rather than pass silently.
+    let nodes = nemesis_nodes().unwrap_or_else(|| {
+        panic!(
+            "tier1_jepsen_metadata: WYRD_TIER1_NEMESIS_NODES is absent/empty — no partition \
+             nemesis was injected. Run via `cargo xtask meta-jepsen`, which draws the \
+             quorum-safe plan through the wyrd-testkit seam and pauses those PD nodes."
+        )
+    });
+    eprintln!(
+        "tier1_jepsen_metadata: nemesis partitions PD node(s) {nodes:?} (quorum-safe minority)"
+    );
+    run(endpoints);
+}
+
+#[cfg(feature = "tikv")]
+fn run(endpoints: Vec<String>) {
+    use futures_util::future::join_all;
+    use std::sync::Arc;
+    use wyrd_traits::{CommitOutcome, MetadataStore, WriteBatch};
+
+    const RACERS: usize = 8;
+
+    let runtime = tokio::runtime::Builder::new_multi_thread()
+        .worker_threads(4)
+        .enable_all()
+        .build()
+        .expect("tokio runtime");
+
+    runtime.block_on(async move {
+        let namespace = format!("wyrd-tier1-jepsen/{}/", std::process::id()).into_bytes();
+        let store = Arc::new(
+            wyrd_metadata_tikv::TikvMetadataStore::connect(endpoints)
+                .await
+                .expect("connect to TiKV")
+                .with_namespace(namespace),
+        );
+
+        let key = b"inode:1".as_slice();
+        // Seed the key at v0 so every racer shares the same precondition.
+        assert_eq!(
+            store
+                .commit(WriteBatch::new().require_absent(key).put(key, &b"v0"[..]))
+                .await
+                .expect("seed commit"),
+            CommitOutcome::Committed,
+        );
+
+        // N racers each CAS v0 → "w{i}", concurrent with the runner's partition nemesis
+        // (a minority of PD nodes paused). TiKV's transactional CAS is what must make
+        // exactly one win, even as the nemesis partitions a minority mid-race.
+        let racers = (0..RACERS).map(|i| {
+            let store = Arc::clone(&store);
+            async move {
+                store
+                    .commit(
+                        WriteBatch::new()
+                            .require(key, &b"v0"[..])
+                            .put(key, format!("w{i}").into_bytes()),
+                    )
+                    .await
+            }
+        });
+        let outcomes = join_all(racers).await;
+
+        let mut winners = 0;
+        for outcome in &outcomes {
+            match outcome {
+                Ok(CommitOutcome::Committed) => winners += 1,
+                Ok(CommitOutcome::Conflict) => {}
+                Err(e) => panic!("a losing racer must be Ok(Conflict), never Err: {e}"),
+            }
+        }
+        assert_eq!(
+            winners, 1,
+            "exactly one concurrent writer wins the CAS under partition"
+        );
+
+        // clause 2 — linearizability of the commit point: the committed value is what every
+        // subsequent reader observes, and it is one of the racers' writes (the winner's).
+        let final_value = store
+            .get(key)
+            .await
+            .expect("read-after-commit")
+            .expect("present");
+        let final_value = String::from_utf8(final_value.to_vec()).expect("utf8");
+        assert!(
+            final_value.starts_with('w'),
+            "the committed value must be the winner's write, got {final_value:?}"
+        );
+        // Read-after-commit is stable (linearizable point): a second read agrees.
+        let again = store.get(key).await.unwrap().unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(
+            again.as_ref(),
+            final_value.as_bytes(),
+            "commit point is stable"
+        );
+    });
+}
+
+#[cfg(not(feature = "tikv"))]
+fn run(endpoints: Vec<String>) {
+    let _ = endpoints;
+    eprintln!(
+        "tier1_jepsen_metadata: WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS is set but the crate was built without \
+         `--features tikv` — skipping. Run it via `cargo xtask meta-jepsen`."
+    );
+}
diff --git a/crates/metadata-tikv/tests/tier1_metadata_integration.rs b/crates/metadata-tikv/tests/tier1_metadata_integration.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4da48fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/metadata-tikv/tests/tier1_metadata_integration.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+//! **Tier-1 metadata integration** (M4.6, #257; proposal 0015 §"DST and tests" →
+//! "Integration", §"Suggested PR sequence" item 6) — the realism-ladder Tier-1 leg for
+//! the redb→TiKV **metadata backend swap**.
+//!
+//! Where the M2/M3 `crates/chunkstore-grpc/tests/tier2_integration.rs` proves the
+//! *chunkstore* data path against real containers, this leg proves the *metadata swap*:
+//! the **same system** — the production `MetadataStore` trait — runs on a real
+//! containerized TiKV cluster behind the **unchanged** trait, and multi-key atomic
+//! create / rename / delete are **all-or-nothing** (proposal 0015: "the bare composition
+//! swap: the same system runs on TiKV behind the unchanged trait; multi-key atomic
+//! create/rename/delete succeed").
+//!
+//! It is **gated** exactly like the sibling tier tests: `#[ignore]` keeps it out of the
+//! unprivileged `cargo xtask ci` (`cargo test --workspace` still COMPILES and type-checks
+//! the body — an API regression on `MetadataStore` would fail to build), and it
+//! additionally no-ops when `WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS` is unset, so a laptop / PDCA worktree
+//! with no TiKV skips cleanly and the gate stays green. It is run by the privileged
+//! `cargo xtask meta-integration` job (`WYRD_TIER1=1`), which stands up the `deploy/`
+//! TiKV, exports its PD endpoints, and runs this with `--ignored --features tikv`.
+
+/// The PD (Placement Driver) endpoints, or `None` when TiKV is not configured —
+/// identical gate to `tests/conformance.rs` so the whole family skips together.
+fn pd_endpoints() -> Option<Vec<String>> {
+    match std::env::var("WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS") {
+        Ok(raw) if !raw.trim().is_empty() => Some(
+            raw.split(',')
+                .map(|e| e.trim().to_string())
+                .filter(|e| !e.is_empty())
+                .collect(),
+        ),
+        _ => None,
+    }
+}
+
+#[test]
+#[ignore = "Tier-1: needs a real containerized TiKV — run via `cargo xtask meta-integration`"]
+fn multi_key_create_rename_delete_atomic_on_tikv() {
+    let Some(endpoints) = pd_endpoints() else {
+        eprintln!(
+            "tier1_metadata_integration: WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS unset — skipping (clean skip; \
+             the gate stays green without a TiKV). Run `cargo xtask meta-integration`."
+        );
+        return;
+    };
+    run(endpoints);
+}
+
+#[cfg(feature = "tikv")]
+fn run(endpoints: Vec<String>) {
+    use wyrd_traits::{CommitOutcome, MetadataStore, WriteBatch};
+
+    let runtime = tokio::runtime::Builder::new_current_thread()
+        .enable_all()
+        .build()
+        .expect("tokio runtime");
+
+    runtime.block_on(async move {
+        let namespace = format!("wyrd-tier1-integration/{}/", std::process::id()).into_bytes();
+        let store = wyrd_metadata_tikv::TikvMetadataStore::connect(endpoints)
+            .await
+            .expect("connect to TiKV")
+            .with_namespace(namespace);
+
+        // Logical keys standing in for `core`'s inode + dirent records — this leg drives
+        // the trait primitive directly (no `core` dep), which is the atomicity surface
+        // the milestone retires the trait-leak on.
+        let inode = b"inode:1".as_slice();
+        let dirent_a = b"dirent:/a".as_slice();
+        let dirent_b = b"dirent:/b".as_slice();
+
+        // ---- create: two keys, all-or-nothing, guarded by require_absent ----
+        let created = store
+            .commit(
+                WriteBatch::new()
+                    .require_absent(inode)
+                    .require_absent(dirent_a)
+                    .put(inode, &b"v1"[..])
+                    .put(dirent_a, &b"1"[..]),
+            )
+            .await
+            .expect("create commit");
+        assert_eq!(created, CommitOutcome::Committed, "create must commit");
+        // Read-after-commit: both keys are visible.
+        assert_eq!(store.get(inode).await.unwrap().as_deref(), Some(&b"v1"[..]));
+        assert_eq!(
+            store.get(dirent_a).await.unwrap().as_deref(),
+            Some(&b"1"[..])
+        );
+
+        // ---- all-or-nothing: a batch with ONE failing precondition writes NOTHING ----
+        let rejected = store
+            .commit(
+                WriteBatch::new()
+                    .require(inode, &b"WRONG"[..]) // stale precondition → Conflict
+                    .put(inode, &b"v2"[..])
+                    .put(b"dirent:/c".as_slice(), &b"1"[..]),
+            )
+            .await
+            .expect("rejected commit is Ok(Conflict), never Err");
+        assert_eq!(
+            rejected,
+            CommitOutcome::Conflict,
+            "stale precondition conflicts"
+        );
+        assert_eq!(
+            store.get(b"dirent:/c".as_slice()).await.unwrap(),
+            None,
+            "a conflicted batch must leave NONE of its puts (all-or-nothing)"
+        );
+        assert_eq!(
+            store.get(inode).await.unwrap().as_deref(),
+            Some(&b"v1"[..]),
+            "the conflicted batch must not have mutated the inode"
+        );
+
+        // ---- rename /a → /b: delete old dirent + put new, atomic under preconditions ----
+        let renamed = store
+            .commit(
+                WriteBatch::new()
+                    .require(dirent_a, &b"1"[..])
+                    .require_absent(dirent_b)
+                    .delete(dirent_a)
+                    .put(dirent_b, &b"1"[..]),
+            )
+            .await
+            .expect("rename commit");
+        assert_eq!(renamed, CommitOutcome::Committed, "rename must commit");
+        assert_eq!(store.get(dirent_a).await.unwrap(), None, "old name is gone");
+        assert_eq!(
+            store.get(dirent_b).await.unwrap().as_deref(),
+            Some(&b"1"[..])
+        );
+        assert_eq!(
+            store.get(inode).await.unwrap().as_deref(),
+            Some(&b"v1"[..]),
+            "rename leaves the inode untouched"
+        );
+
+        // ---- delete: remove dirent + inode atomically ----
+        let deleted = store
+            .commit(
+                WriteBatch::new()
+                    .require(dirent_b, &b"1"[..])
+                    .require(inode, &b"v1"[..])
+                    .delete(dirent_b)
+                    .delete(inode),
+            )
+            .await
+            .expect("delete commit");
+        assert_eq!(deleted, CommitOutcome::Committed, "delete must commit");
+        assert_eq!(store.get(dirent_b).await.unwrap(), None, "dirent removed");
+        assert_eq!(store.get(inode).await.unwrap(), None, "inode removed");
+    });
+}
+
+#[cfg(not(feature = "tikv"))]
+fn run(endpoints: Vec<String>) {
+    let _ = endpoints;
+    eprintln!(
+        "tier1_metadata_integration: WYRD_TIKV_PD_ENDPOINTS is set but the crate was built \
+         without `--features tikv` — skipping. Run it via `cargo xtask meta-integration`."
+    );
+}
